{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791051381,"nonce":"Y6ANTe61vMGGjQVdhlDRtMu7u8E=","title":"Hot reload accepts a class-attribute edit in an ashui template, then segfaults in reloaded code","message":"An ashui window program (tools/demo/Reloading.hx in ashui) run with `ash --mode hybrid --hot-reload`. Swapping in a build whose only source change is two Tailwind class edits in a component template (`text-lg font-bold` -\u003e `text-lg font-bold text-primary` on a text, `px-3 py-1 rounded-md` -\u003e `px-4 py-1 rounded-full` on a div) and a heading string passes the function-table shape check, then:\n\n    [hot-reload] propagating 1006 field patch(es) to live heap objects\n    [hot-reload] reloaded 363 changed function(s)\n    === CRASH: SIGSEGV (signal 11) fault_addr=0x1b ...\n      #0 jit findex=1398 (llvm+0x19) Fun_1398\n\nRSS reached about 5 GB during the reload (NUC, 6.8 GB). A heading-only edit (heading.hl) reloads fine: 1 field patch, 56 functions, state kept.\n\nBuilds (compiled by Haxe on the Mac, same flags), in /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/ashui/.ashui/hot-reload-repro (Mac) and ~/.cache/ashui-nuc/reload (NUC, with the Linux hdlls beside them):\n- before.hl: the program as started\n- classes.hl: the crashing edit\n- heading.hl: the heading-only edit that works\n- Reloading.before.hx: the source of before.hl\n\nReproduce on the NUC, in the seat0 session (WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-0 XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000):\n\n    cd ~/.cache/ashui-nuc/reload \u0026\u0026 cp before.hl Reloading.hl\n    RELOADING_SCRIPT=1 LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$PWD:$HOME/.cache/ash-nuc ~/.cache/ash-nuc/ash --mode hybrid --hot-reload $PWD/Reloading.hl \u0026\n    # after 'ready' is printed:\n    cp classes.hl Reloading.next.hl \u0026\u0026 mv Reloading.next.hl Reloading.hl\n\nAsh: the NUC's ~/.cache/ash-nuc/ash (built 2026-10-03 13:30, has the shape check). Not yet tried on the Mac. Expected: either the reload applies, or it is refused with a reason and the old code keeps running.","files":null}]}